      "explanation": "The original fractions require \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\) to be nonzero. Combining the left side over the common denominator \\(xy\\) gives a single fraction equal to \\(1/z\\):\n\\[\n\\frac1z=\\frac1x-\\frac1y=\\frac{y-x}{xy}.\n\\]\nSince \\(1/z\\ne0\\), we also have \\(y-x\\ne0\\). Both sides are therefore nonzero, so taking reciprocals is valid and gives\n\\[\nz=\\frac{xy}{y-x}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice D.",
      "id": "combine-and-invert",
